      "description": "View from Michni Post at Khyber Pass near Torkham border crossing.\nThe picture depicts the tunnels of the Khyber Pass Railway (abandoned section Landi Kotal–Torra Tigga) in the Khyber Agency near Torkham, the area which is the border and main trade route between Pakistan and Afghanistan. The road is the Khyber Pass (part of the N-5, and Grand Trunk Road) that joins Peshawar, Pakistan, with Kabul, Afghanistan. One of the most historical passes of the world as Alexander the Great entered the subcontinent through this route.",
